## Approved Test Plan
{step:plan}

**Always materialize the suite-vs-code sync gate first**: copy `coverage-check.ts` from your knowledge file verbatim to `.pi/api-tests/coverage-check.ts` (it fails when production code changed but the suite did not, AND when a changed route has no real call in the runtime coverage snapshot, so a stale-but-green suite cannot slip through).

**If `.pi/api-tests/` already exists, modify it in place**: keep every existing case/scenario that still passes, add only the missing test points, and reuse the existing lib/types/prep APIs. Do not regenerate files that already work — diff your change against the existing suite.

Otherwise create the suite. Implement the strongly-typed TypeScript test suite under `.pi/api-tests/` (runner.ts + lib/ + types/ + prep.ts + cases/*.test.ts + scenarios/*.test.ts + baselines/*.json + reports/) exactly as the reference implementation in your knowledge file prescribes:
1. Place the pure TypeScript helpers in `.pi/api-tests/lib/` (client.ts, route-coverage.ts, failure.ts, assert.ts, diff.ts, context.ts, reporter.ts) verbatim from the knowledge file - `client` must call `RouteCoverage.record(...)` on every request and every assertion must throw `AssertionFailure` with a failure code.
2. Define strong TypeScript interfaces in `.pi/api-tests/types/` for request DTOs and response schemas.
3. Implement Scenario Chains with typed context for step-by-step dependency passing, covering full state machine lifecycles (Create -> Read -> Optimistic Lock 409 -> Archive -> Pin Binding -> Anti-Drift -> Teardown).
4. Implement Dual-Service Diffing via `Assertions.assertDiff` when candidate URL is configured.
5. Implement Dataset Matrix iteration (`legacy` vs `new_feature`) when requested.
6. Use `client.switchProfile` and gateway headers for multi-tenant / auth testing.
7. Resolve runtime prerequisites in `prep.ts`, storing them into `ctx.set(key, val)`; never hardcode environment-specific ids in test cases.
8. Write `.pi/secrets/api.env.local.json` (chmod 600) with credentials and resolve runtime settings from it. Credentials live ONLY in `.pi/secrets/` or environment variables - never inline a token into any file under `.pi/api-tests/`. 
9. Ensure `runner.ts` auto-discovers `cases/*.test.ts` + `scenarios/*.test.ts` (directory scan via `discoverSuites()`, NEVER a hand-maintained import list), writes `.pi/api-tests/reports/route-coverage.json` in `finally`, and writes `.pi/api-tests/reports/latest-summary.md`.
9b. Every case file exports exactly ONE `run*` function and records results only via `reporter.pass(...)` / `reporter.fail(name, dataset, err, meta)` - never hand-rolled `addResult` literals, otherwise the failure triple {code, message, diagnostic} and the runtime route binding are lost. Every route from the changed-route inventory must actually be called at least once; if a route genuinely needs no test, record it in `.pi/api-tests/coverage-allowlist.json` as {pattern, reason} - an empty reason does not count.
Write the resolved request settings (base URL / auth / tenant) into `.pi/secrets/api.env.local.json` so subsequent runs resolve them without prompting. Also persist the gathered baseline mode as `API_BASELINE_MODE`: `自动…`→`auto`, `强制对比…`→`verify`, `重新记录基线`→`record`, `不做…`→`off`. Credentials must only live in `.pi/secrets/api.env.local.json` or environment variables — never inlined into suite sources and never in your output.
